{
  "title": "Best Time to Buy and Sell Stock",
  "description": "`prices[i]` is the price of a share on day `i`.\n\nYou may make **at most one** purchase and **at most one** sale, and the sale must happen on a later day than the purchase. Return the largest profit you can make. If no profitable trade exists, return `0`.\n\n### Examples\n\n| `prices` | Result | Why |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `[7, 1, 5, 3, 6, 4]` | `5` | Buy at 1 on day 1, sell at 6 on day 4 |\n| `[7, 6, 4, 3, 1]` | `0` | Prices only fall; never trade |\n| `[2, 4, 1]` | `2` | Buy at 2, sell at 4 |\n\n### Constraints\n\n- `1 <= prices.size() <= 1000`\n- `0 <= prices[i] <= 10000`\n- Inputs are passed as function arguments and the answer is returned from the function. Do not read from standard input or print the result.\n",
  "reference": "int max_profit(vector<int> prices) {\n    int best = 0;\n    int lowest = prices[0];\n    for (int price : prices) {\n        lowest = min(lowest, price);\n        best = max(best, price - lowest);\n    }\n    return best;\n}\n",
  "template": "int max_profit(vector<int> prices) {\n    // Return the best profit from a single buy followed by a single sell.\n    return 0;\n}\n",
